<a href="../Articles/Halbach_Array.php" class=articles>&nbsp;&#149;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Halbach Array&nbsp;</a><br>
<ul class=art>
<li><font class=title2><strong>Klaus Halbach</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;, a retired physicist of Lawrence Berkely National Laboratory, created a unique magnetic array that has become fundamental in passive levitation<br>
<br>
Originally invented for use in particle accelerators, this device is the fundamental principle behind the Inductrack MAGLEV system, a levitating train that requires no power to levitate; power is only used to create forward motion. The Halbach arrays repel buried loops of wire after they have been accelerated to speed, lifting the train. 
